								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=984"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14015#msg14015"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14015#msg14015">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #31 on:</b> January 28, 2005, 09:40:33 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Garadan,<br /><br />Are you serious.<br />&quot;I had to basically lay down the law and be a real asshole to start weeding out those that were gonna follow and those that couldnt (ie Rogosh, Galamir, and whatever that retarded rangers name was that came from forsaken... started with a K ) &quot;<br /><br />I left because ascent wasnt going anywhere with a clueless leader like you. One who couldnt lead a mouse to cheese.<br />You were dead in the water without all the forsaken recruits towards the end. <br />Old ascent /salute, garadan /rude. <br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
