							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ascent was actually very lucky where Forsaken was not. When I joined at the beginning of the summer, about 3 months after Forsaken disbanded, Ascent was working on building up forces and strengths after losing a portion of their core of hard-core people.&nbsp; Honch was the leader he was grouchy and discouraged because a lot of his friends moved on.&nbsp; After deciding he was done was when I saw how incredible Ascent truly was.<br /><br />Ascent was lucky because of the amount of skilled people I saw who were willing and able to pick up and keep us going over and over as they exhausted themselves.&nbsp; I saw so many people step-up and refuse to be the suck and stop the raids when the leadership lacking. It was amazing.&nbsp; From Garadan to Snnaakes and Karadana, Katia, Draybard, Bealt, Vay, Averiel .... and especially Fysts, with his efforts in the end. It was incredible how much talent was evident and I really admired them all for their loyalties. <br /><br />Rogosh and Theorax were both incredible leaders and held in high regard by the members of Forsaken but when Forsaken lost the two of them and keeneye within 4 days of each other and we crumbled like dust in the wind.&nbsp; Nobody could or would&nbsp; step up and fill those shoes and honestly I think that if someone had we&#039;d of disbanded anyway because nobody had the confidence and commitment to stay and follow a possible sinking ship. Their shoes were too awesome to fil so nobody&nbsp; even tried.<br /><br />I enjoyed both experiences and I am proud to have been a member of Forsaken and Ascent. I couldn&#039;t say one guild was better than the other because they both rocked in their own ways and were unforgettable.&nbsp; <br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />My character will be guildless the next time I log in.&nbsp; I will be sad disbanding and I know it&#039;s the last time I am probably going to be in a guild. I&#039;ve seen way too many guilds disband lately and&nbsp; I don&#039;t want to start over with another grueling application process. I cringe at the thought of starting over in friendships and dkp&#039;s for the 3rd time this year.&nbsp; <br /><br />I&#039;d like to wish the remaining guilds on RN the best of luck and successes. As for Ascent and Forsaken.. /salute.. /cheer.. /hug.. and it&#039;s no big deal. It&#039;s just &quot;<i>another one gone.. another one gone.. another one bites the dust..</i>&quot;&nbsp; &nbsp;So don&#039;t let it get you too! 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
