								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1395.msg14035#msg14035">Re: Ascent breaking up?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #39 on:</b> January 28, 2005, 11:26:40 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							So many old school ascent left when I took over...&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/bullshit.gif" alt="Bull Shit!" border="0" /> They had already left before I even returned to the game. They left when Delheru left you dumb shit. What your failing to realize is when you were around in ascent is when we were rebuilding. So ya raids might of not gone as fast and smooth as it could have. Once the rebuilding stage was pretty much handled we progressed. We were two kills from Anguish. And really if rl didnt get so out of control and I was still playing, no doubt in my mind we would get those two trials beat. You think your some big shit because you managed to get forsaken to potime.... way behind schedule. <br /><br />You keep saying grow a sack... for what? Nothing you have said holds any true value. While you were tagged Ascent you acted like you still were a leader of forsaken. Always running your mouth. That was your problem. That was why you were annoying. You werent any big asset to the guild. You werent a main tank, hell you caused more drama then you ever did any good. You can think I acted like it was all about me, shit I dont care. I listened to what my other officers had to say. Your god damn right I didnt listen to you, if you ever had said anything worth listening too maybe I would have. <br /><br />Keep posting though with your lame shit. Its amusing enough to read. 
						</td>
					</tr>
